# STRATA 8.6.8 — POST-BATCH-A EXECUTION DISPATCH / B1 + BATCH-C ORACLE

Fresh Current remains BIG #703/5971366932 with mirror IRIS #3/5971369301.

IBA succession update:
IBA 1.8 has been succeeded by IBA 1.9.

This succession does NOT move implementation ownership into IBA.

## IBA 1.9 role

`IBA_1_9_ROLE = SUCCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE_CUSTODIAN / NO_ACTIVE_IMPLEMENTATION_OWNERSHIP`

IBA 1.9 should:
- reconstruct the accepted Batch-A constitution and preserve it;
- answer only genuine semantic/architecture ambiguities routed back from Development/Professor/STRATA;
- prevent local implementation choices from becoming new semantics;
- avoid reopening Founder design;
- avoid serial patch-review work;
- remain STOPPED/standby unless a named constitutional question is returned.

## Lane B — dispatch now

`OWNER_B = BIG-OFFICE-DEVELOPMENT / CDA-owned authorized Builder substrate`

`TASK_B = B1_SHARED_SEMANTIC_KERNEL`

Consume:
- STRATA Batch-A acceptance #703/5971366932;
- frozen Batch-A package at commit `dbde4cea846fa9c7c8a4ad7094f360db318eb292`;
- artifact 18 Implementation Repair Dependency Graph;
- artifacts 01, 07, 13, 15, 16 and impacted-surface inventory 19.

B1 scope ONLY:
- A1 epistemic/domain algebra;
- A2 explicit identity/relation/causal-occurrence primitives;
- A4 shared lifecycle/effect reducers needed as kernel primitives;
- temporal/as-of primitives;
- semantic validators;
- explicit representation maps.

B1 prohibitions:
- no B2-B6 early implementation;
- no downstream caller patching outside B1 dependency needs;
- no replacement-E1 mutation;
- no Pilot execution/scoring;
- no new policy;
- no production merge/deploy;
- no continuity ON;
- no authority expansion.

Required B1 return:
- branch/base/head/tree;
- exact changed surfaces;
- Batch-A contract mapping;
- B2 type/schema representation plan;
- focused conformance evidence;
- full regression evidence;
- residual blockers;
- `STRATA_RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED`.

## Lane C — dispatch now

`OWNER_C = PROFESSOR / STRATA-ORCHESTRATED FRESH INDEPENDENT ORACLE AUTHOR`

`TASK_C = BATCH_C_INDEPENDENT_ORACLE_DERIVATION`

Consume only:
- frozen Batch-A package;
- permitted founding/Blueprint/source evidence;
- sealed audit as falsification/traceability evidence;
- preserved candidate-independent evaluation inputs where required.

Remain blind to:
- repaired candidate outputs;
- implementation-authored expected results;
- score-derived configuration.

Required products:
- A1-A5 truth tables/state machines/mutation matrices;
- Executive Reasoning observable-product oracle;
- Filtration/ICCP round-trip/loss/privacy/currentness oracle;
- Functional Perception oracle;
- IEF phase-floor/maturity oracle;
- whole-stack counterexample set;
- executed legacy-proof disposition register;
- frozen independent oracle/proof package.

Implementation != oracle derivation != independent acceptance.

## Progress accounting

Batch A remains CLOSED.

Current downstream state:
`B1_RELEASED / BATCH_C_ORACLE_RELEASED / NO_NEW_GATE_PROGRESS`

Next progress occurs only when a downstream acceptance gate closes.

